course: dictionary
lesson: 1365
title: Noun or verb: canoe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can work as different parts of speech. A noun names a thing, and a verb shows an action. Canoe can be both. «Long before any European ship arrived, Polynesian navigators crossed the Pacific in double canoes.» Here canoe is a noun, because it names a thing: a light, narrow boat that you move with a paddle.
explain: Canoe can also be an action. To canoe means to paddle or travel in a canoe. «Children go canoeing on the lake with an instructor.» Canoeing shows what the children are doing, so it works as a verb.
explain: To tell which one it is, look at the job the word does. Try putting «the» in front of it. «The canoe» works, so canoe is a noun. «To canoe» or «canoeing» shows an action, so it is a verb.
fact: A canoe is a light, narrow boat, pointed at both ends, that you move with a paddle.
fact: To canoe means to travel or paddle in a canoe.
fact: «Paddle your own canoe» is a phrase that means look after yourself.
fact: Words such as canoe came into English from the Taíno language.
fact: Canoes were built for travel and fishing by First Nations peoples and by Maori in New Zealand.
exercise: «Polynesian navigators crossed the Pacific in double canoes.» In this sentence, what kind of word is canoe? | A place | A verb, an action | *A noun, a thing | An adjective, describing a word
exercise: «Mia wants to canoe on the lake this summer.» What does canoe mean here? | *To paddle a canoe along the water | A kind of fish | A large ship for carrying cargo | A light, narrow boat
exercise: Which sentence uses canoe as a noun? | «Canoeing is fun for everyone.» | «They canoed across the bay.» | *«We carried the canoe down to the river.» | «We like to canoe on Sundays.»
test: Which phrase means look after yourself? | Count the paddles | Sink the canoe | Canoe in the rain | *Paddle your own canoe
test: In «Polynesian sailors crossed thousands of kilometres of the Pacific Ocean in canoes», what kind of word is canoes? | An adjective, describing a word | *A noun, more than one canoe | A place name | A verb, an action
exam: Which word in «Children go canoeing on the lake with an instructor» is a verb? | *canoeing | children | lake | instructor
